+        # array under the GIL. For multi-GB tensors that copy is the dominant
+        # cost. Stream the raw buffer in big chunks via memoryview instead.
+        #
+        # Only real ndarrays go down this path. LazyChunkedTensor is not an
+        # ndarray and must never be materialized into one -- it is used for
+        # tensors too large to hold in memory (the Qwen4Exp PLE n-gram table is
+        # 102 GB) and streams itself one row-chunk at a time. Handing it to
+        # np.ascontiguousarray() silently yields a 1-element *object* array,
+        # i.e. 8 bytes, so the tensor is declared at full size in the header and
+        # 8 bytes land in the file.
